# Prelude No. 3 in C-sharp major, Well-Tempered Clavier I, BWV 848
# (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: quick, bright and airy, one beat to the bar. A broken-chord
# figure in sixteenths runs in one hand while the other answers in
# eighths, and every eight bars the hands swap jobs. Late in the piece
# the figure gives way to a long dominant pedal and a free, toccata-like
# close. It should skip, not hurry.
#
# Time signature and bars: 3/8, 104 bars, no upbeat; the MIDI has the
# same 104 bars.
#
# Tempo: dotted quarter = 76, one beat per bar (eighth = 228), 104
# beats, about 1:22. Track times (MusicBrainz track lists): Angela
# Hewitt (Hyperion, 1998) 1:24, about 74; Edwin Fischer 1:21, about 77;
# Rosalyn Tureck 1:17 (older set), about 81; Sviatoslav Richter 1:14,
# about 84; Friedrich Gulda 1:11, about 88; Glenn Gould 1:05 and Tureck
# (2002 issue) 1:04, about 96. 76 sits with Hewitt and Fischer: the
# sixteenths (about 7.6 a second) stay clean on the chip, and the
# piece still has a one-in-a-bar lilt.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score, checked bar by bar against the
# MIDI; the eight-bar exchange of the hands is plain in both; the key
# plan is my reading of the bass):
#   1-8    figure in the right hand, C-sharp major.
#   9-16   the hands exchange: figure in the left hand, toward
#          G-sharp major.
#   17-24  figure in the right hand, G-sharp major (the dominant).
#   25-32  figure in the left hand.
#   33-54  shorter exchanges through the minor keys (D-sharp minor,
#          A-sharp minor) and on to the subdominant, F-sharp major
#          (47-54).
#   55-62  the opening eight bars return in C-sharp major.
#   63-86  a new texture: the hands in eighths over a G-sharp pedal
#          (63-75), then sequences that tighten toward the dominant.
#   87-97  the dominant pedal on G-sharp: broken chords in the left
#          hand, single notes in the right.
#   98-104 a free close: runs passed between the hands, and the final
#          C-sharp major chord.
#
# Range: the dominant pedal G-sharp 2 (bars 87-99) and the last bass
# notes sit below the chip's B2 and are lifted an octave, so the pedal
# sounds at G-sharp 3; the build in those bars is carried by the ramp.

tempo 76 4.          # dotted quarter, one beat to the 3/8 bar

voice mid 0          # two lines, figure and answer: no inner voice

dyn 1 mf             # bars 1-8: the figure on top, the home key
dyn 9 mp             # bars 9-16: hands exchanged, an echo on the
                     # second manual
dyn 17 mf            # bars 17-24: the figure on top, G-sharp major
dyn 25 mp            # bars 25-32: hands exchanged again
dyn 33 mp            # bars 33-54: the minor keys, staying quiet
dyn 55 f             # bars 55-62: the opening returns, full
dyn 63 mp            # bars 63-75: the new eighth-note texture over the
                     # pedal, softer to leave room
ramp 76-86 mf        # bars 76-86: the sequences tighten
ramp 87-97 f         # bars 87-97: the dominant pedal, the last build
dyn 98 f             # bars 98-104: the free close

rit 4 0.75           # the last four bars into the final chord
